WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.100
(light music)

00:00:01.100 --> 00:00:02.420
- [Narrator] Utilizing one of the most

00:00:02.420 --> 00:00:04.789
efficient natural camouflages on earth,

00:00:04.789 --> 00:00:07.491
this is the pink winged stick insect.

00:00:07.491 --> 00:00:09.991
(light music)

00:00:12.800 --> 00:00:15.410
True to its name, the
pink winged stick insect

00:00:15.410 --> 00:00:17.500
does resemble a stick.

00:00:17.500 --> 00:00:18.720
They have been observed making

00:00:18.720 --> 00:00:20.620
repetitive side-to-side movements,

00:00:20.620 --> 00:00:23.590
mimicking a stick blowing in the wind.

00:00:23.590 --> 00:00:25.810
As camouflage is their biggest defense,

00:00:25.810 --> 00:00:27.950
many stick insects are nocturnal

00:00:27.950 --> 00:00:31.140
and in the face of an
attack, will play dead.

00:00:31.140 --> 00:00:35.440
Some have been seen to even
shed a limb to evade a predator.

00:00:35.440 --> 00:00:39.590
Long and thin, these insects
range between 13 and 21 inches

00:00:39.590 --> 00:00:42.840
in length, with females
being longer than the males.

00:00:44.110 --> 00:00:46.820
Little is known about stick
insects, making it difficult

00:00:46.820 --> 00:00:50.000
to declare the vulnerability
of their status in the wild.

00:00:50.000 --> 00:00:53.380
However, this one is endemic to Madagascar

00:00:53.380 --> 00:00:55.800
and was listed as an endangered species

00:00:55.800 --> 00:00:59.192
due to aggressive
deforestation in the area.

00:00:59.192 --> 00:01:02.152
This is the pink winged stick insect.

00:01:02.152 --> 00:01:04.652
(light music)

